# Code Patterns

## Required Imports
```csharp
using UnityEngine;
using Sirenix.OdinInspector;  // Odin Inspector
using DG.Tweening;           // DOTween (when using animations)
using static Enumerations;   // Project enums
```

## Standard Debug Pattern (REQUIRED)
Use LogExtensions for consistent logging across all components:
```csharp
#region Debug
[FoldoutGroup("Debug"), SerializeField] 
private bool enableDebugLogs = true;

[FoldoutGroup("Debug"), Button("Log Status"), ShowIf("enableDebugLogs")]
private void LogCurrentStatus() => this.Log($"Status: {GetDebugStatus()}", enableDebugLogs);

// Use extension methods from LogExtensions.cs:
// this.Log("message", enableDebugLogs);           → [ClassName] message
// this.LogWarning("message", enableDebugLogs);    → [ClassName] message
// this.LogError("message");                       → [ClassName] message (always logs)
// this.LogStateChange("state", old, new, flag);   → [ClassName] state changed: old → new
// this.LogAction("action", "details", ms, flag);  → [ClassName] action: details (ms)
// this.LogPerformance("op", count, ms, flag);     → [ClassName] PERF - op: count in ms
#endregion
```

### Logging Categories (from LogExtensions.cs)
- **CRITICAL (keep ON)**: StageManager, WaveManager, GridManager, PlayerManager
- **NOISY (safe to disable)**: CubeCollisionManager, MarkerVisualManager, AudioManager
- **MODERATE (case-by-case)**: WaveSegmentController, GridRowManager, ScoreManager

## Odin Inspector Patterns

### Inspector Organization
```csharp
// Use Title for major sections (replaces [Header] for top-level)
[Title("Configuration")]
[SerializeField] private float speed = 5f;

// Use FoldoutGroup for collapsible sections
[FoldoutGroup("Advanced Settings")]
[SerializeField] private bool useAdvanced = false;

// Use BoxGroup for visual grouping without collapse
[BoxGroup("Timing")]
[SerializeField] private float duration = 1f;

// Use TabGroup for complex inspectors
[TabGroup("Tabs", "General")]
[SerializeField] private string displayName;

[TabGroup("Tabs", "Combat")]
[SerializeField] private int damage;
```

### Conditional Display
```csharp
// Show/hide based on bool
[ShowIf("useAdvanced")]
[SerializeField] private float advancedMultiplier;

// Show/hide based on enum
[ShowIf("cubeType", CubeType.Matrix)]
[SerializeField] private Vector2Int areaSize;

// Enable/disable (grayed out but visible)
[EnableIf("isInitialized")]
[SerializeField] private bool canActivate;
```

### Validation & Buttons
```csharp
// Required field validation
[Required("Prefab must be assigned!")]
[SerializeField] private GameObject prefab;

// Range with info box
[MinValue(0), MaxValue(100)]
[SerializeField] private int percentage;

// Inspector buttons
[Button("Initialize", ButtonSizes.Large)]
public void Initialize() { /* ... */ }

[Button("Test Feature"), GUIColor(0.4f, 0.8f, 1f)]
private void TestFeature() { /* ... */ }

// Button row
[ButtonGroup("Actions")]
[Button("Start")] private void Start() { }
[ButtonGroup("Actions")]
[Button("Stop")] private void Stop() { }
```

### Lists & Collections
```csharp
// Searchable list (for large collections)
[Searchable]
[SerializeField] private List<WaveData> waves;

// Table display for data lists
[TableList(ShowIndexLabels = true)]
[SerializeField] private List<SpawnEntry> spawnEntries;

// Inline editor for ScriptableObjects
[InlineEditor]
[SerializeField] private StageData stageData;
```

### Common Odin Attributes Reference
| Attribute | Purpose |
|-----------|---------|
| `[Title("Name")]` | Section header with line |
| `[FoldoutGroup("Name")]` | Collapsible section |
| `[BoxGroup("Name")]` | Visual box grouping |
| `[TabGroup("Tab", "Name")]` | Tabbed sections |
| `[ShowIf("condition")]` | Conditional visibility |
| `[Required]` | Validation - must be set |
| `[Button("Label")]` | Inspector button |
| `[TableList]` | Display list as table |
| `[Searchable]` | Add search to lists |
| `[InlineEditor]` | Expand SO in inspector |
| `[ReadOnly]` | Display but don't edit |
| `[InfoBox("msg")]` | Help text in inspector |

## Manager Reference Pattern
```csharp
#region Manager References
private WaveManager waveManager;
private GridManager gridManager;
#endregion

private void Start()
{
    CacheManagerReferences();
    ValidateReferences();
}

private void CacheManagerReferences()
{
    // Prefer singleton when available
    gridManager = GridManager.Instance;
    
    // Or FindFirstObjectByType in Start() ONLY
    waveManager = WaveManager.Instance ?? FindFirstObjectByType<WaveManager>();
}

private void ValidateReferences()
{
    if (waveManager == null)
        this.Log("WaveManager not found - features limited", enableDebugLogs);
}
```

### CRITICAL: Anti-Patterns to Avoid
These patterns caused bugs in production - found in CubeManager, PlayerManager:
```csharp
// BAD: Runtime lookup - caused NullReferenceExceptions
private void MoveForward() {
    var waveManager = FindFirstObjectByType<WaveManager>(); // NEVER DO THIS
}

// BAD: Lookup in frequently called method
private void HandleTileChange() {
    var actionManager = FindFirstObjectByType<PlayerActionManager>(); // NEVER DO THIS
}
```
Always cache in Start(), use cached reference everywhere else.

## Singleton Pattern (When Approved)
```csharp
#region Properties
public static ManagerName Instance { get; private set; }
#endregion

#region Unity Lifecycle
private void Awake()
{
    if (Instance == null)
    {
        Instance = this;
    }
    else if (Instance != this)
    {
        Debug.LogWarning($"Multiple {GetType().Name} found! Destroying duplicate.");
        Destroy(gameObject);
        return;
    }
}

private void OnDestroy()
{
    if (Instance == this)
    {
        Instance = null;
    }
}
#endregion
```

## Enumerations Usage
Always use static import for Enumerations:
```csharp
using static Enumerations;

// Then use directly:
CubeType.Unit
MarkerMode.Unit
GameAudioEvent.WaveStarted
```

## POC (Proof of Concept) Marking
```csharp
// POC: Quick implementation for testing - may need refinement
public void TemporaryFeature()
{
    // Functional but not optimized
}
```
- POC code must be functional even if not optimized
- POC code must be marked with `// POC:` comment
- POC code has no upgrade requirement - if it works, it works
